Fix the four reported UI issues; split large controllers

1. Find in Files: "Replace with" gets its own labelled row with a 240 pt
   minimum-width field (it collapsed to a sliver when sharing the toggles
   row); panel minimum size added
2. Dark-theme checkerboard strip: Scintilla paints folding margins with a
   chrome-coloured pattern unless the fold-margin colours are set; both are
   now the gutter background. New pixel-level regression test renders the
   editor offscreen and fails on the pattern (verified by temporarily
   reverting the fix: luminance 0.99 -> test fails)
3. Tab accessibility: each tab is an accessible element (radio-button role,
   label, selected value, press action, "Close Tab" custom action); strip is
   a tab group; close buttons labelled per tab
4. Narrow windows: responsive find bar hides optional controls (Find All,
   in-selection, whole word, count) as width shrinks; pure-logic layout
   rules are unit tested
Also: AppCoordinator menu handlers and MainWindowController delegates +
FileDropView split into focused files; performance docs updated with measured
evidence that the blank-window baseline is AppKit, not the editor engine
(Welcome screen with no Scintilla view measures the same).
168 tests green.
